{
 "en": [
  {
   "text": "Ever let an AI code suggestion take over without thinking?",
   "start": 0.63,
   "end": 3.784,
   "rows": 3,
   "font": 54,
   "direction": "ltr",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    200,
    994,
    434
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "You see a suggestion pop up and hit Tab, trusting it feels easy.",
   "start": 4.3,
   "end": 8.061,
   "rows": 3,
   "font": 54,
   "direction": "ltr",
   "bbox": [
    72,
    200,
    1007,
    434
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "But that shortcut can hide gaps in how you actually understand the code.",
   "start": 8.881,
   "end": 12.464,
   "rows": 3,
   "font": 54,
   "direction": "ltr",
   "bbox": [
    121,
    200,
    959,
    434
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Metacognition means watching your own thinking, catching when you’re just going along.",
   "start": 12.95,
   "end": 17.152,
   "rows": 3,
   "font": 54,
   "direction": "ltr",
   "bbox": [
    65,
    200,
    1015,
    434
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "When you accept a suggestion blindly,",
   "start": 17.971,
   "end": 19.804,
   "rows": 2,
   "font": 54,
   "direction": "ltr",
   "bbox": [
    56,
    200,
    1024,
    356
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "you skip the mental check that reveals whether it truly fits.",
   "start": 20.054,
   "end": 23.031,
   "rows": 3,
   "font": 54,
   "direction": "ltr",
   "bbox": [
    101,
    200,
    979,
    434
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "That missing check is the gap between feeling confident and actually knowing.",
   "start": 23.852,
   "end": 27.566,
   "rows": 3,
   "font": 54,
   "direction": "ltr",
   "bbox": [
    60,
    200,
    1019,
    434
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Seeing the gap makes you decide whether to",
   "start": 28.388,
   "end": 30.34,
   "rows": 2,
   "font": 54,
   "direction": "ltr",
   "bbox": [
    120,
    200,
    960,
    356
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "adapt the suggestion or rewrite it your way.",
   "start": 30.352,
   "end": 32.614,
   "rows": 2,
   "font": 54,
   "direction": "ltr",
   "bbox": [
    160,
    200,
    919,
    356
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "In Koder, the CLI offers a one‑line fix as soon as you type a function name.",
   "start": 33.09,
   "end": 37.518,
   "rows": 3,
   "font": 54,
   "direction": "ltr",
   "bbox": [
    96,
    200,
    984,
    434
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "If you just press Enter, you get the code but",
   "start": 38.337,
   "end": 40.563,
   "rows": 2,
   "font": 54,
   "direction": "ltr",
   "bbox": [
    110,
    200,
    970,
    356
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "you miss the chance to ask why it works.",
   "start": 40.575,
   "end": 42.587,
   "rows": 2,
   "font": 54,
   "direction": "ltr",
   "bbox": [
    98,
    200,
    981,
    356
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Next time Koder suggests, pause and read the suggestion out loud.",
   "start": 43.1,
   "end": 46.862,
   "rows": 3,
   "font": 54,
   "direction": "ltr",
   "bbox": [
    124,
    200,
    955,
    434
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Then ask yourself: does this solve the problem, and can I explain each part?",
   "start": 47.681,
   "end": 51.847,
   "rows": 3,
   "font": 54,
   "direction": "ltr",
   "bbox": [
    81,
    200,
    998,
    434
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Write a quick comment summarizing the logic before you accept –",
   "start": 52.669,
   "end": 55.873,
   "rows": 3,
   "font": 54,
   "direction": "ltr",
   "bbox": [
    86,
    200,
    993,
    434
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "that forces the mental check.",
   "start": 56.05,
   "end": 57.514,
   "rows": 1,
   "font": 54,
   "direction": "ltr",
   "bbox": [
    78,
    200,
    1001,
    278
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Try this pause‑and‑explain habit with Koder on your next commit.",
   "start": 58.0,
   "end": 61.119,
   "rows": 3,
   "font": 54,
   "direction": "ltr",
   "bbox": [
    60,
    200,
    1020,
    434
   ]
  }
 ],
